  "body": "OPEN HOME | SAT & SUN | 11:00 – 11:45\r\n\r\nRemember when family homes came with backyards, room for the boat, oversized double garaging and plenty of space for the kids to play? Those were the Auckland homes many of us grew up in and they're becoming increasingly difficult to find.\r\n\r\nWelcome to 13 Katui Street, a wonderful reminder of traditional Kiwi family living, beautifully reimagined for today.\r\n\r\nPositioned on an elevated 612sqm freehold corner site, this substantial two storey brick and weatherboard home offers something increasingly rare; a generous flat section, beautifully renovated family with breathtaking views.\r\n\r\nThis renovation is nothing short of exceptional. Meticulously transformed throughout to an incredibly high standard, the home showcases outstanding attention to detail, quality finishes and thoughtful design at every turn. From the beautifully appointed new kitchen and luxurious bathrooms to the double glazing, ducted climate control and refined interior finishes, no expense appears to have been spared in creating a home that feels contemporary, sophisticated and ready to enjoy. All while retaining the generous proportions and practicality of its original design.\r\n\r\nAnd then there are the views. Sweeping panoramas stretch from Auckland's CBD skyline across Milford Beach, the Marina to Rangitoto Island and the sparkling Hauraki Gulf.\r\n\r\nProperty highlights\r\n• Classic 1970s Kiwi home  \r\n• Beautifully transformed throughout\r\n• Four bedrooms | three bathrooms | three living areas\r\n• Substantial 310sqm (approx.) family home\r\n• Spectacular views | from the Gulf to CBD\r\n• Oversized internal garage | with ducted climate control \r\n• Ample off street parking for the boat or jet skis\r\n• Room for children | pets | and a potential future swimming pool (subject to approvals)\r\n• Top school zones | Campbells Bay Primary | Double Westlake\r\n\r\nHomes like this are becoming harder to replace. Not simply because of their size or location, but because they offer something a modern development so often leaves behind: space to live, room to grow and the freedom to enjoy your own piece of the beautiful North Shore.\r\n\r\nThe current CV is not reflective of this home's extensively renovated condition.",
